action,x,y,origin,button,key,micros,note,platform
# P19 on GtkBackend on macOS (TEST_BACKEND=gtk4): one menu, every item kind; the toggle and the button item are chosen with the pointer, because the keyboard start position in a GTK popover menu varies between runs (queue item 22).
# The keys are the AppKit file's (the first Down selects Button item here too; measured 2026-10-16). One difference: GTK keeps a popover menu open after a check item -- GtkModelButton pops down only for a plain item -- so the AppKit file's second open closed the menu instead and the last Down/Return chose "second button item". Escape closes it first.
# 按鍵與 AppKit 檔相同;唯一差別是 GTK 在勾選項目之後不關閉選單(只有一般項目會),所以先按 Escape 關閉。
click,72,232,frame,left,,,Open the menu,macos
sleep,,,,,,1200000,let it open,macos
click,99,344,frame,left,,,"Toggle item, with the pointer -- toggle item -> true. Not the keyboard: the first Down started on Button item in some runs and on Toggle item in others, and a reopened menu drew Button item highlighted while one Down chose Second button item (2026-10-16); queue item 22",macos
sleep,,,,,,500000,,macos
key,,,,,escape,,GTK keeps the menu open after a check item,macos
sleep,,,,,,700000,let the menu close,macos
click,72,232,frame,left,,,Open the menu again,macos
sleep,,,,,,1200000,let it open,macos
click,98,271,frame,left,,,"Button item, with the pointer -- the capture must read last action -> button item and toggle item -> true",macos
sleep,,,,,,1200000,let the menu close,macos
